---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
---

<Layout
  title="Child safety · Dipity"
  description="Dipity's standards against child sexual abuse and exploitation, and how to report it.">
  <article class="prose mx-auto px-5 pt-10 sm:px-8">
    <h1>Child safety standards</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Dipity, made by Coracle Social LLC ("Coracle", "we"), does not allow child sexual abuse and
      exploitation of any kind.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Effective October 12, 2026.</strong></p>

    <h2>What is prohibited</h2>
    <p>You may not use Dipity to create, share, request or promote:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>child sexual abuse material, including drawn, edited or generated imagery;</li>
      <li>sexualized content involving anyone under 18;</li>
      <li>grooming, or any attempt to contact a minor for a sexual purpose;</li>
      <li>sextortion, or threats to share intimate images of a minor;</li>
      <li>the trafficking or sexual exploitation of children in any form.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Agreeing to this is a condition of using Dipity, and is part of our <a href="/terms"
        >terms of use</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Where posts go</h2>
    <p>
      Dipity has no servers. Posts pass directly from phone to phone over Bluetooth, and a post can
      travel at most two hops from the person who wrote it, though a phone that receives it may be
      anywhere by then. We never receive, host or review what people post, and we cannot delete a
      post from anyone's phone.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can do in the app</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Flag a post</strong> from its menu, choosing "Illegal" or another reason. Your phone
        stops passing a post on as soon as you flag it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Mute, block and suppress the author</strong> from the same dialog. Your phone stops
        accepting their posts, stops passing them on, and sends them nothing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Report to Dipity</strong> from the flag dialog. Your mail app opens with a message to
        us naming the post and its author.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Please never attach a picture, or a screenshot, of anything showing a child. Sending it on is
      distributing it, even to us. Naming the post is enough.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do with a report</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We read every report sent to <a href="mailto:safety@coracle.social">safety@coracle.social</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        We report apparent child sexual abuse material to the National Center for Missing &amp;
        Exploited Children (NCMEC), as US law requires, and to other authorities where the law
        requires it.
      </li>
      <li>We cooperate with law enforcement investigating child exploitation.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We comply with the child safety laws that apply to Dipity and to Coracle.</p>

    <h2>If a child is in danger</h2>
    <p>
      If a child is in immediate danger, call your local emergency number first. You can also
      report child sexual exploitation directly to NCMEC's <a href="https://report.cybertip.org"
        >CyberTipline</a
      > or by phone at 1-800-843-5678, or outside the US to a hotline listed by <a
        href="https://www.inhope.org">INHOPE</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Our child safety point of contact is reachable at <a href="mailto:safety@coracle.social"
        >safety@coracle.social</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
